                <pb facs="0471" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg459"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.199/58: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Seville</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-01T18:00:00-05:00">December 1, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your November 20, 9 a.m. In view of continued delay in granting of safe conduct
                    for Chapman’s return to Bilbao, he has been authorized to return to the United
                    States on leave, unless before his departure, probably within a week, such
                    permit is granted. Please report as soon as possible result of action promised
                    by General Queipo de Llano.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
